// expect: 12
// SYNTAX §«Field access» — `u.name` lowers to a field load whose offset
// the receiver's type resolves at compile time. Named `name` against a
// record whose other field sorts EARLIER, so a slot-keyed read would
// answer 30 and a name-keyed read answers 12.
//
// This is the control that made the pattern finding precise: field
// access through the same record is correct, which is why the
// param-receiver defect is the PATTERN's and not the record's.
fn main() = {
  let u = {age: 30, name: 12}
  u.name
}
